    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "c4HlI",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 56319,
      "name": "Annotation — S5-12 Shortfall vs exhaustion (not UI)",
      "width": 390,
      "stroke": "$--annotation",
      "strokeWidth": {
        "left": 2
      },
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 6,
      "padding": [
        10,
        12
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ERxkl",
          "name": "Label",
          "fill": "$--annotation",
          "content": "ANNOTATION · NOT IN THE UI",
          "fontFamily": "$--font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "700",
          "letterSpacing": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "n4imGA",
          "name": "Annotation",
          "fill": "$--annotation",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "A shortfall (14 units can't fund a required come bet of 10 plus 10 in odds) keeps spec 1's funding pause: legal override, Collect instead or Stop strategy, never a rebuy, resize or top-up. After settlement a cheaper compatible strategy or table may use the rest. Exhaustion (S5-13) happens only when no legal opening wager at any launch table configuration can be funded. Even 4 units is still a shortfall, because roulette inside bets and craps proposition bets accept 1 unit.",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$--font-ui",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
